{
  "case_id": "2021-20-828",
  "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The state secrets privilege is firmly grounded in the Constitution and the common law and is critical to safeguarding the national security."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Kneedler, do you place -- a -- few times in your opening remarks you referred to this as a common law privilege. Is that your argument, that it's based in common law rather than inheres in executive power?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the case should be dismissed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Arulanantham",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ARULANANTHAM: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Defendants do not seek just to exclude secret information from this case. If that were true, there would have been no need for them to file a motion to dismiss our religion claims. Instead, what they seek is not just to exclude information but also to dismiss it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0004-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the main reason is because, if you look at Section 1806(g), which is the provision which authorizes relief in the case, once the district court has determined that the surveillance either was or was not lawfully authorized and conducted, it says you suppress the evidence or otherwise grant the motion in accordance with the requirements of law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about this -- the -- the \"grant the motion in accordance with law\" language that you just mentioned? In -- \"in accordance with law,\" does that include in accordance with the state secrets privilege?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Where does Article II fit into your analysis? Because Judge Bumatay and then Judge Diaz on the Fourth Circuit both started with an Article II backdrop and the roots of the state secrets privilege"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0004-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court still dismissed the whole thing without ever looking to see whether --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I just wonder, why would Congress put such significant language stuck in this provision? Isn't that an oblique way to have the consequences you're ascribing to that language?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0005-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: I do have a question. It's a follow-up to something Justice Alito asked you earlier. He said to posit, you know, you have religion claims in the suit, and the suit is about whether the surveillance violated or discriminated on the basis of religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. But my question is then, what happens to the individual defendants? Let's say the evidence that they can use to defend themselves against the claim that they religiously discriminated is in this body of evidence that's protected by the state secrets doctrine. And you're saying dismissal's not a remedy, so they just go in with their hands tied behind their back and they just are sitting ducks?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Arulanthanam",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0006-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ARULANANTHAM: Yes. So -- so two thoughts, Your Honor. Under common law, that is certainly the result, and there are --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0006-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF EDWIN S. KNEEDLER ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "63561d050342e748e538db8d31c0e0b9b76301c129c158016443d84a4cf26426",
      "evidence_id": "ev-63561d050342-0006-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 136,
        "start": 136
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's what happens if the privilege is validly asserted and the evidence is removed from the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 0.0,
